---
import SiteLayout from '~/layouts/SiteLayout.astro';

// NOTE FOR MAINTAINERS
// This policy describes what the site actually does as built: a Web3Forms
// contact form, FareHarbor bookings, Cloudflare Pages hosting, Google Fonts,
// Unsplash images, Google Analytics, and Google Ads measurement. Google
// Analytics is configured via analytics.vendors.googleAnalytics.id in
// config.yaml. If you add another analytics tag, a pixel, or a chat widget,
// update the "Information collected automatically" and "Advertising"
// sections and bump LAST_UPDATED. Have counsel review before relying on this
// document.

const LAST_UPDATED = 'August 25, 2026';

const metadata = {
  title: 'Privacy Policy',
  description:
    'How San Diego Trail Company collects, uses, and protects your information when you use sandiegotrailcompany.com, contact us, or book a ride in Poway, CA.',
  robots: { index: true, follow: true },
};

const h2 = 'font-family:\'Cormorant Garamond\',serif;font-size:clamp(24px,3vw,32px);font-weight:400;color:#3b2314;';
const h3 = 'font-size:17px;font-weight:600;color:#3b2314;';
---

<SiteLayout metadata={metadata}>
  <!-- Header band (dark so the transparent nav stays readable) -->
  <section class="px-6 lg:px-12 pt-32 pb-16 lg:pt-40 lg:pb-20" style="background-color:#3b2314;">
    <div class="max-w-[900px] mx-auto">
      <div class="uppercase tracking-[0.2em] mb-4" style="font-size:11px;color:#8a9e7b;">Legal</div>
      <h1
        class="text-white mb-5"
        style="font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',serif;font-size:clamp(44px,7vw,72px);font-weight:300;line-height:1.05;"
      >
        Privacy Policy
      </h1>
      <p class="text-white" style="font-size:16px;opacity:0.75;">Last updated: {LAST_UPDATED}</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="px-6 lg:px-12 py-16 lg:py-24" style="background-color:#f5f0e8;">
    <div
      class="max-w-[900px] mx-auto flex flex-col gap-10"
      style="font-size:16px;line-height:1.8;color:#2c2c2c;"
    >
      <p>
        This policy explains what San Diego Trail Company (&ldquo;we,&rdquo; &ldquo;us,&rdquo; &ldquo;our&rdquo;)
        collects when you visit <strong>sandiegotrailcompany.com</strong>, send us a message, or book an experience
        with us &mdash; and what we do with it. We have tried to write it in plain language rather than legal padding.
      </p>

      <div>
        <h2 style={h2} class="mb-4">Who we are</h2>
        <p>
          San Diego Trail Company operates a working ranch in Poway, California, offering guided horseback trail rides,
          riding lessons, kids camps, ranch stays, and equine-assisted coaching. You can reach us at:
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4">
          14875 Mina De Oro, Poway, CA 92064<br />
          <a href="tel:+18587486441" style="color:#c49a3c;">858-748-6441</a><br />
          <a href="mailto:ride@powayequestriancenter.com" style="color:#c49a3c;" class="break-all"
            >ride@powayequestriancenter.com</a
          >
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 style={h2} class="mb-4">Information you give us</h2>
        <h3 style={h3} class="mt-4 mb-2">Contact form</h3>
        <p>
          When you use the form on our <a href="/contact/" style="color:#c49a3c;">contact page</a>, we collect your name,
          email address, an optional phone number, the subject you select, and your message. Submissions are delivered
          to our inbox by <strong>Web3Forms</strong>, a third-party form-relay service. We use these details only to
          answer you.
        </p>
        <h3 style={h3} class="mt-6 mb-2">Bookings and payments</h3>
        <p>
          Rides, lessons, camps, stays, and gift certificates are booked and paid for through <strong>FareHarbor</strong>,
          our reservation provider. FareHarbor collects the booking and payment information needed to process your
          reservation, under its own privacy policy. <strong
            >We never see or store your full payment card number.</strong
          >
        </p>
        <h3 style={h3} class="mt-6 mb-2">Talking to us directly</h3>
        <p>
          If you call, email, or message us on social media, we keep what you send so we can help you and maintain a
          record of the conversation.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 style={h2} class="mb-4">Information collected automatically</h2>
        <p>
          Our site is hosted on <strong>Cloudflare Pages</strong>. Like essentially all web hosting, Cloudflare records
          technical request data &mdash; IP address, browser and device type, referring page, and timestamps &mdash; to
          serve the site, defend against attacks and bots, and diagnose faults.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4">Loading a page also makes requests to a small number of outside services:</p>
        <ul class="mt-3 flex flex-col gap-2 pl-5" style="list-style:disc;">
          <li>
            <strong>Google Fonts</strong> (fonts.googleapis.com, fonts.gstatic.com) supplies our typefaces. Google
            receives your IP address as part of that request.
          </li>
          <li><strong>Unsplash</strong> (images.unsplash.com) serves some photography on the site.</li>
          <li>
            <strong>Google Analytics</strong> (googletagmanager.com) collects standard usage data &mdash; pages
            viewed, referring site, device/browser type, and approximate location &mdash; to help us understand how
            visitors use the site.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-4">We do not operate a social media tracking pixel on this site.</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 style={h2} class="mb-4">Cookies and local storage</h2>
        <p>
          We do not set our own advertising cookies. Your browser may store a small display preference locally on your
          device so the site renders consistently; this stays on your device and is not transmitted to us. Google
          Analytics sets cookies to distinguish visitors and sessions, Cloudflare may set cookies strictly necessary
          for security and load balancing, and Google may set cookies in connection with the advertising described
          below. You can clear or block cookies in your browser settings, though blocking strictly necessary cookies
          may affect how the site works.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 style={h2} class="mb-4">Advertising</h2>
        <p>
          We advertise through <strong>Google Ads</strong>. If you reach our site by clicking one of our ads, the link
          may carry a click identifier (for example a <em>gclid</em> parameter) that lets Google report whether the ad
          led to a booking or an inquiry. This tells us that an ad worked; it does not tell us who you are.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4">
          Google may use its own cookies and identifiers for ad measurement and remarketing under its policies. You can
          review and adjust these at
          <a href="https://myadcenter.google.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color:#c49a3c;"
            >Google My Ad Center</a
          >
          and
          <a
            href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            style="color:#c49a3c;">Google&rsquo;s partner-sites policy</a
          >.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 style={h2} class="mb-4">How we use your information</h2>
        <ul class="flex flex-col gap-2 pl-5" style="list-style:disc;">
          <li>To answer questions and respond to inquiries you send us.</li>
          <li>To arrange, confirm, and deliver rides, lessons, camps, stays, and events.</li>
          <li>To operate, secure, and troubleshoot the website.</li>
          <li>To measure whether our advertising is working.</li>
          <li>To meet legal, tax, insurance, and safety obligations.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-4">
          <strong>We do not sell your personal information, and we do not share it with third parties for their own
            marketing.</strong>
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 style={h2} class="mb-4">Who we share it with</h2>
        <p>We share information only with the service providers that make the ranch and this site run:</p>
        <ul class="mt-3 flex flex-col gap-2 pl-5" style="list-style:disc;">
          <li><strong>FareHarbor</strong> &mdash; reservations and payment processing.</li>
          <li><strong>Web3Forms</strong> &mdash; delivering contact form submissions to our inbox.</li>
          <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> &mdash; website hosting, delivery, and security.</li>
          <li><strong>Google</strong> &mdash; analytics, advertising measurement, and font delivery.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-4">
          We may also disclose information where the law requires it, or where it is necessary to protect the safety of
          our guests, our staff, or our horses.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 style={h2} class="mb-4">Your California privacy rights</h2>
        <p>
          If you are a California resident, the CCPA as amended by the CPRA gives you the right to know what personal
          information we hold about you, to request a copy, to ask us to correct or delete it, and not to be treated
          differently for exercising those rights. Because we do not sell or share personal information for
          cross-context behavioral advertising, there is no sale to opt out of.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4">
          To make a request, email
          <a href="mailto:ride@powayequestriancenter.com" style="color:#c49a3c;" class="break-all"
            >ride@powayequestriancenter.com</a
          > or call 858-748-6441. We may need to verify your identity before acting, and we will respond within the time
          the law allows.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 style={h2} class="mb-4">Children</h2>
        <p>
          We run camps and programs for children, but this website is intended for adults and we do not knowingly
          collect personal information online from children under 13. Registration for youth programs is completed by a
          parent or guardian, who provides the participant&rsquo;s details along with any medical or emergency
          information we need to keep that child safe. If you believe a child has given us information online without a
          parent&rsquo;s involvement, contact us and we will delete it.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 style={h2} class="mb-4">How long we keep it</h2>
        <p>
          We keep inquiries and booking records for as long as needed to serve you and to satisfy our legal, tax,
          insurance, and safety obligations &mdash; then we dispose of them. Waivers, incident records, and minors&rsquo;
          program paperwork are retained longer where law or our insurers require it.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 style={h2} class="mb-4">Security</h2>
        <p>
          The site is served over HTTPS, and we rely on established providers for hosting, forms, and payments. No
          method of transmission or storage is completely secure, so we cannot guarantee absolute security &mdash; but
          we do not collect payment card details ourselves, which removes the most sensitive category of data from our
          hands entirely.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 style={h2} class="mb-4">Links to other sites</h2>
        <p>
          Our site links out to FareHarbor, Google Maps, and our social media profiles. Once you follow a link, that
          organization&rsquo;s privacy policy governs what happens to your information. We are not responsible for
          their practices.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 style={h2} class="mb-4">Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          If we change how we handle information &mdash; for example by adding analytics or a new booking tool &mdash;
          we will update this page and revise the date at the top. Material changes will be made clear rather than
          buried.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 style={h2} class="mb-4">Contact us</h2>
        <p>Questions about this policy, or about information we hold on you:</p>
        <p class="mt-4">
          San Diego Trail Company<br />
          14875 Mina De Oro, Poway, CA 92064<br />
          <a href="tel:+18587486441" style="color:#c49a3c;">858-748-6441</a><br />
          <a href="mailto:ride@powayequestriancenter.com" style="color:#c49a3c;" class="break-all"
            >ride@powayequestriancenter.com</a
          >
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
